From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cera <cera@local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:25:31 -0700
Subject: fix(dart): correct the callback vtable ABI and support async delivery

Two changes to the same renderer, kept in one patch because they interleave
within the bridge body and neither compiles without the other.

RustBuffer argument ABI: UniFFI passes String / Sequence / Enum / Record /
Option to a foreign callback as a RustBuffer BY VALUE, not as a Pointer<Utf8>
holding JSON. Confirmed against the Kotlin and Swift reference bindings, where
these arguments are RustBuffer.ByValue. Adds callback-specific FFI mappers,
deliberately scoped to callback bridges so the non-ffibuffer runtime path keeps
its existing String mapping, and decodes through the existing binary reader.
Rust transfers ownership of each lowered buffer to the callback, so the bridge
frees them; without that every invocation leaked one.

Cross-thread delivery: a void vtable method of an interface used by an async API
is invoked from a non-isolate thread, where NativeCallable.isolateLocal is
undefined behaviour. Those now use NativeCallable.listener. Methods with a
return value must answer synchronously by writing outReturn, which only
isolateLocal can do, so they stay isolate-local and therefore same-thread only.
